<div class="evidneuro-case-study">
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-challenge">
    <p class="section-label">The challenge</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-challenge">Similar language does not mean equivalent evidence</h2>
      <p>
        Scientific search can conflate findings: it can treat nearby wording as interchangeable
        even when the underlying species, brain region, cell type, intervention, or experimental
        condition differs. A result about the mouse hippocampus, for example, should not
        automatically become evidence for an apparently similar human finding. EvidNeuro treats
        those conditions as part of the claim rather than disposable context.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section pipeline-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-pipeline">
    <p class="section-label">Pipeline</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-pipeline">From source documents to auditable evidence</h2>
      <p>
        The intended architecture is a linked evidence ladder. Captured documents can be archived,
        normalized, and inspected today; interpretation and the complete automatic path through
        every downstream layer are still being integrated.
      </p>

      <figure class="evidence-ladder">
        <ol aria-label="EvidNeuro evidence pipeline">
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">Source</span>
            <div><strong>Scientific PDF</strong><small>The original document remains the source of truth.</small></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">Capture</span>
            <div><strong>Layout-aware source blocks</strong><small>Text, geometry, reading order, tables, figures, equations, captions, and source references.</small></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">L0</span>
            <div><strong>Evidence objects</strong><small>Stable, source-bound objects preserve document structure instead of flattening it into generic chunks.</small></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">L1</span>
            <div><strong>Claims and measurements</strong><small>Conditioned assertions and numeric results retain links to their supporting evidence.</small></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">L2</span>
            <div><strong>Topics, methods, and experiments</strong><small>Claims can belong to several groupings rather than a single rigid hierarchy.</small></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-code">L3</span>
            <div><strong>Provenance-bound synthesis</strong><small>Consensus, disagreement, open questions, and timelines retain references to lower layers.</small></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <figcaption>
          A six-stage path from the original PDF to synthesis. The lower source and evidence layers
          remain available as higher-level structure is added.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-provenance">
    <p class="section-label">Provenance</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-provenance">Every result should remain drillable</h2>
      <p>
        Stable identifiers and explicit source spans connect each layer. Page geometry and document
        structure preserve the context of tables, figures, captions, and equations, while
        claim-bearing prose stays distinct from surrounding material. When interpretation is
        uncertain, the system records a named warning or withholds the passage rather than
        substituting generated text for evidence.
      </p>

      <figure class="provenance-chain">
        <ol aria-label="Provenance path from synthesis to the source PDF">
          <li>Synthesis</li>
          <li>Claim</li>
          <li>Evidence object</li>
          <li>Source block</li>
          <li>PDF region</li>
        </ol>
        <figcaption>Synthesis → claim → evidence object → source block → PDF region.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-domain">
    <p class="section-label">Domain model</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-domain">Retrieval that respects experimental identity</h2>
      <p>
        Domain information is carried with evidence instead of added only after retrieval.
        Supporting mappings can connect original language to resources such as UBERON, Cell
        Ontology, and Allen Brain Map without erasing the wording used by the paper.
      </p>

      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Species and brain regions</h3>
          <p>Retain identity information needed to separate otherwise similar findings.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Ontology-backed normalization</h3>
          <p>Connect surface forms to canonical concepts and external identifiers while preserving the source wording.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Conditions and evidence strength</h3>
          <p>Carry experimental context, evidence type, null findings, and reproducibility information with claims.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Contradictions and measurements</h3>
          <p>Preserve opposing findings and structured numeric results instead of collapsing them into one summary.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-system">
    <p class="section-label">System</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-system">A retrieval engine built around evidence bundles</h2>
      <p>
        The system combines lexical and vector retrieval, reciprocal-rank fusion, and optional
        reranking, then returns structured evidence bundles rather than a loose collection of text
        fragments. Tool choices support that evidence flow rather than define it.
      </p>
      <dl class="system-list">
        <div><dt>Service layer</dt><dd>TypeScript services and HTTP APIs</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Document path</dt><dd>Background PDF parsing and MinerU-based layout capture</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Retrieval</dt><dd>BM25 and vector search joined with reciprocal-rank fusion</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Storage</dt><dd>File-backed development storage with PostgreSQL and pgvector options</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Review</dt><dd>An inspection and labeling workspace for human decisions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Output</dt><dd>Evidence bundles with provenance-aware retrieval results</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-current-state">
    <p class="section-label">Current state</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-current-state">Built in stages, with unresolved work kept visible</h2>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Automatic source interpretation and evidence construction are under active development.</li>
        <li>Captured documents are archived, normalized, and inspectable; newly captured documents do not yet automatically complete the full evidence-to-synthesis ladder.</li>
        <li>Model-proposed document joins are recorded for review rather than applied automatically.</li>
        <li>Ambiguous or contaminated passages can be withheld instead of promoted as claim evidence.</li>
        <li>Evaluation is internal and ongoing, using frozen document sets and human-reviewed references.</li>
        <li>Broader corpus coverage and retrieval-quality validation remain future work.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-next">
    <p class="section-label">Next</p>
    <div class="section-body">
      <h2 id="evidneuro-next">What comes next</h2>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Connect the remaining evidence-to-claim ingestion path.</li>
        <li>Improve handling of ambiguous document boundaries and mixed caption/body content.</li>
        <li>Expand human-reviewed claim-quality evaluation.</li>
        <li>Validate on fresh document families without tuning against held-out material.</li>
        <li>Prepare the technical report/manuscript.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="closing-status" aria-labelledby="evidneuro-status-title">
    <p>Project status</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="evidneuro-status-title">Work in progress</h2>
      <p>
        The repository is private, and a technical report/manuscript is in preparation.
        Screenshots and a public demo will be added only when the system and evaluation are ready
        for release.
      </p>
      <small>Work in progress · Private repository · Report/manuscript in preparation</small>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

